      "title": "‘Politics can be brutal’: Sarah Hanson-Young speaks out about divisions within Greens",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/01/politics-can-be-brutal-sarah-hanson-young-speaks-out-about-divisions-within-greens",
      "description": "<p>Greens sources say the relationship between new leader David Shoebridge and runner-up Mehreen Faruqi is seriously strained</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/29/larissa-waters-resignation-greens-leadership-contenders\">Sarah Hanson-Young</a> has spoken out about major divisions in the Greens party room, offering support to newly elected leader David Shoebridge and describing politics as “brutal”.</p><p>The South Australian senator contested Wednesday’s leadership ballot, finishing behind Shoebridge and outgoing deputy leader, Mehreen Faruqi.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/01/politics-can-be-brutal-sarah-hanson-young-speaks-out-about-divisions-within-greens\">Continue reading...</a>",
